[size=5][b]Quest and Exploration Navigation - Fork[/b][/size]
[b]Version 0.8.6-fork.1 | Experimental[/b]
Show routes to quests, map pins and collectibles on the regional map, then follow a guiding thread in the game world.

This community fork is based on [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/phantombladezero/mods/472]azqwq333's Quest and Exploration Navigation 0.8.5-beta[/url] and the local-fix5 patches. It adds route checks, local obstacle detours, fixes for traversal connections and target sync with Map Tracker Plus (UE4SS) 1.0.9.

The original author has stopped maintaining the mod. kurosakana maintains this fork independently. azqwq333 created the original navigation system, all 11 world graphs, the walking-surface datasets and the original bundled assets. This fork does not imply endorsement by the original author.

[size=4][b]Changes from upstream[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Route checks.[/b] Check that the ground supports the route and that the player character has enough room to pass (capsule clearance). Compare feasible walking distances in three dimensions and reject fallback paths that are known to be blocked.
[*][b]Local detours.[/b] Try to route around rocks and other obstacles within about 120 m. While searching, or if a search fails, the map keeps the checked part of the route, an X at the blockage and a dashed tail for the unchecked remainder. The world thread stops at the end of the checked section.
[*][b]Collectible approach points.[/b] Guide the player to interaction range on the same floor as the item. Account for uneven ground so that a straight height interpolation is not mistaken for a floor change.
[*][b]Traversal connections.[/b] Connect recognized ladders, climbs, rope/grapple links, slides and lifts. Check their direction and unlock state. You still perform each traversal action yourself.
[*][b]World thread.[/b] Replace the original trailing particles with a thin-line mesh that appears immediately. Keep its endpoints above ground and limit collision checks on distant sections and repeated updates.
[*][b]Map Tracker Plus 1.0.9 sync.[/b] Use an adapter included with navigation to sync selected targets, target changes, collection and cancellation. Hover over an item and middle-click to select it with its actual height preserved.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements and exact compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Required:[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/phantombladezero/mods/113]PBZModLoader 1.0.0 (#113)[/url].
[*][b]Optional settings menu:[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/phantombladezero/mods/149]Mods Menu 0.7.2 (#149)[/url].
[*][b]For collectible navigation:[/b] separately install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/phantombladezero/mods/187]Map Tracker Plus - Minimap and Collectibles (UE4SS) 1.0.9 (#187)[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/phantombladezero/mods/5]UE4SS for Phantom Blade Zero 1.0.3 (#5)[/url]. The collector's download folder is named Map Collectible Tracker.
[/list]

[b]Exact runtime required for collectible sync:[/b] v3.0.1-1195-g1ceefac8 Shipping. The adapter checks the runtime and collector entry-file hashes. With other builds, collectible sync is disabled; core quest and map-pin navigation remain available.

[b]What works with 1.0.9:[/b] manual and automatic targets, target switching, collection completion, cancellation sync and middle-click selection that preserves item height.

[b]What has not been ported from the old JS 0.6.7 integration:[/b] the minimap route overlay, enlarged icons and automatic accessory hints. These navigation settings have no effect on UE4SS 1.0.9. Map Tracker Plus continues to manage its own minimap, icons and tracking.

[b]Do not install both collector generations.[/b]

[size=4][b]Installation / update[/b][/size]
The download is one complete package for PBZModLoader. It does not include PBZModLoader, UE4SS or the collector. A separate package for the Mods Menu folder layout is not provided.
[list=1]
[*]Close the game. If you have used navigation before, back up [b]ProjectPBZ/Content/Paks/~mods/PBZQuestRoute.txt[/b].
[*]Install PBZModLoader. For collectible navigation, also install the exact collector and UE4SS versions listed above.
[*]If updating, disable the original mod or any older navigation copy. Move its old script folder outside the game directory and keep your configuration.
[*]Choose an installation method. [b]Manual:[/b] open the game root through Steam > Manage > Browse local files, then merge the ZIP's ProjectPBZ and platform folders into it. [b]UE Mod Manager:[/b] import the complete ZIP and select both the navigation game files and PBZQuestRouteCompat. Shared paths may cause the manager to identify this as an update to the original mod. Enable only one navigation copy.
[*]If migrating from older layouts, move out the old JS collector folder [b]ProjectPBZ/PBZModLoader/mods/pbz-map-tracker/[/b], the legacy 0.7.x files [b]zzz_PBZQuestRoute_P.pak/.utoc/.ucas[/b], PBZQuestRouteMouse and any other old navigation layouts.
[*]Check that [b]ProjectPBZ/PBZModLoader/mods/PBZQuestRoute/main.js[/b] exists. For collectible sync, also check [b]platform/steam/ue4ss/Mods/PBZQuestRouteCompat/dlls/main.dll[/b]. Start the game normally through Steam.
[/list]
PBZQuestRouteCompat is part of navigation. Keep the original PbzMapTracker files unchanged. This fork uses the original mod's internal install and configuration names and replaces that navigation copy.

[size=4][b]Controls / settings / uninstall[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Quests:[/b] use the game's normal quest tracking.
[*][b]Collectibles (1.0.9):[/b] left-click an item icon to track it, or hover over it and middle-click to navigate while preserving its height.
[*][b]Map pins:[/b] close the filters, then middle-click empty map space to place a ground pin. Hold middle-click on empty space for about 0.6 seconds to cancel.
[*][b]Controller:[/b] use the game's confirmation binding, normally A.
[*][b]World thread:[/b] close the map to see it. WorldThread must be enabled. Sense30 mode requires Sense first.
[*][b]Arrival:[/b] guidance clears when you reach the target on the same floor. Select the target again to restore guidance.
[*][b]Travel actions:[/b] bell travel and traversal actions remain player-controlled.
[/list]

[b]Settings and logs[/b]
[list]
[*]Settings menu: F9 > Quest & Exploration Navigation - Fork.
[*]Configuration: ProjectPBZ/Content/Paks/~mods/PBZQuestRoute.txt.
[*]Startup record: PBZQuestRoute-startup.txt in the actual Saved directory.
[*]Navigation log: ProjectPBZ/Saved/PBZQuestRoute-log.txt.
[*]Adapter status: PBZQuestRouteCompat-status.txt in the adapter's own folder.
[/list]

[b]Uninstall[/b]
Close the game and remove this navigation through the manager. For manual removal, remove these navigation folders:
[list]
[*]ProjectPBZ/PBZModLoader/mods/PBZQuestRoute/
[*]ProjectPBZ/Content/Mods/PBZQuestRoute/
[*]platform/steam/ue4ss/Mods/PBZQuestRouteCompat/
[/list]
Keep your settings, the collector and shared runtimes. To return to the original navigation mod, move out the fork's scripts and adapter before restoring it.

